Experiment :01: To demonstrate Various Data Types and Operators in Python.

Aim : To demonstrate various data types and operators in Python.

Algorithm:
1.Start.
2.Declare variables of different data types.
3.Display their values and data types.
4.Perform basic arithmetic operations.
5.Display the results.
6.Stop.

Program/Code:
a = 10
b = 5
name = "Python"
x = True
print("\nArithmetic Operators:")
print("Addition:", a + b)
print("Subtraction:", a - b)
print("Multiplication:", a * b)
print("Division:", a / b)
print("\nLogical Operators:")
print("AND:", a > 5 and b < 10)
print("OR:", a < 5 or b < 10)
print("NOT:", not x)
print("\nBitwise Operators:")
print("AND:", a & b)
print("OR:", a | b)
print("XOR:", a ^ b)
print("\nAssignment Operators:")
c = a
print("c =", c)
c += b
print("c += b:", c)
c -= b
print("c -= b:", c)
print("\nIdentity Operators:")
p = [1, 2, 3]
q = p
r = [1, 2, 3]
print("p is q:", p is q)
print("p is r:", p is r)
print("p is not r:", p is not r)

